{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-03", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906690, "segment_id": "ILvUwWdmam", "segment_broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Charles Gibson (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 60, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906690, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-03", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906690, "segment_id": "rswXGtwDCP", "segment_broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "segment_title": "Economy: Rescue Package / House Passage / The Bill", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The House passage and presidential signing of the economic rescue plan reported.  \n\n(Capitol HilL: Jake Tapper)  The House vote with many members of Congress switching their vote from when the bill was first defeated featured; vote tally outlined on screen.  [Representatives John BOEHNER, Howard COBLE&#134;, Roy BLUNT&#134;- speak about the vote on the bill.]  Stock Market Report and the market response cited.  \n\n(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The bad employment numbers with lost jobs in August cited.  \n\n(Studio: Betsy Stark)  How the legislated money may be used to break the logjam in the credit market featured; scenes shown of Congressional deliberations; details given about the Emergency Economic Stabilization Act and the need for banks to get credit for their assets so they can start lending.  [Home BUYER, car DEALER, Governor Arnold SCHWARZENEGGER&nbsp- offer views on the financial crisis.]  [PNC Bank chief economist Stuart HOFFMAN&#134;- speaks about the credit and consequences for the economy.]  [ISI economic policy analyst Tom GALLAGHER&#134;, Bankrate.com analyst Greg McBRIDE&#134;- comments on the time for the borrower to see change and the bad loans out there.]  The reasons for the drop of the market after the House vote discussed. ", "segment_duration": 370, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906691, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-03", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906690, "segment_id": "GeJZUfDjb2", "segment_broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "segment_title": "Campaign 2008 / Biden-Palin Debate", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The viewership last night for the vice presidential debate between Senator Joe Biden and Governor Sarah Palin cited.   (New York: Kate Snow)  The relief for the candidates the day after the debate featured.  [On Fox, PALIN&nbsp- criticizes Senator Barack Obama about the war.]  [BIDEN&nbsp- speaks about Senator John McCain.]  [\"Time\" magazine's Mark HALPERIN&nbsp- assesses whether Biden hit the mark and Palin's argument and style.]  [In debate, PALIN&nbsp- speaks about the economy and the surge in Iraq.]   (Studio: Charles Gibson; Washington: George Stephanopoulos)  The strategies for the two sides with one month to go in the election after the vice presidential debate and the passage of the rescue bill, the McCain campaign's decision to pull out of Michigan, how it shows McCain is switching from offense to defense and Obama is campaigning in three key states that usually go Republican discussed.   (Studio: Charles Gibson)  The guests on Sunday's \"This Week\" noted. ", "segment_duration": 280, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63430.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906692, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-03", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906690, "segment_id": "JJOmVDM3Iz", "segment_broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Charles Gibson)", "segment_description": " ", "segment_duration": 30, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63710.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906693, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-03", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906690, "segment_id": "7FEx2xQ4QV", "segment_broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Total; Aveeno; VESIcare; \"Flash of Genius\")", "segment_description": " ", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63740.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906694, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-03", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906690, "segment_id": "34FsOMkJko", "segment_broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "segment_title": "Campaign 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / Georgia", "segment_description": "(Studio: Charles Gibson)  The 50 states in 50 days report re-introduced.  \n\n(Valdosta: Steve Osunsami)  The unprecedented effort in Georgia to register voters and how African Americans have been energized by Senator Barack Obama, but the state will likely go for Senator John McCain, featured; scenes shown from a high school football game in Valdosta and of registration efforts.  [Lowndes County board of elections Deb COX&#134;, high school parents Ricky ROWE&#134;, Laverne ROME&#134;, newly registered voter Pearlie PATTERSON&#134;- talk about registration, the election and the issues.] ", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63870.0", "legacy_segment_id": 906695, "network_name": "ABC", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "broadcast_date": "2008-10-03", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 1, "distributor": 8, "broadcast_title": "World News Tonight", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1700, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 906690, "segment_id": "nThD0N5C3s", "segment_broadcast_id": "lCtZfUI3AQ", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items (Studio: Charles Gibson)", "segment_description": " ", "se